 "segments": [
  "[  0.00-  3.54] If you fall asleep holding two steel balls, you might wake up a genius!",
  "[  3.92-  7.80] You see, first, you put two metal plates on the floor, sit down right above them,",
  "[  7.96- 11.58] and hold a steel ball in each hand. Then, you just let yourself drift off.",
  "[ 11.78- 15.56] Now, here's the weird part. The second you fall asleep, your hands go limp,",
  "[ 15.78- 18.76] the balls smash into the plates, and the noise jolts you awake!",
  "[ 18.98- 22.84] Sounds like the worst nap ever, but Thomas Edison was rumored to do it on purpose.",
  "[ 23.12- 26.92] That's because right before deep sleep, your brain hits a strange halfway state",
  "[ 26.92- 30.86] called hypnagogia, where it starts connecting ideas it never would while you're awake.",
  "[ 31.14- 33.66] Normally, you sink right past it and forget everything,",
  "[ 33.82- 36.02] but the crash yanks you out right in the middle of it,",
  "[ 36.16- 38.62] so you wake up holding the idea instead of the balls."
 ],
